From: MedyMa <75345465+MedyMa@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libreplace: use the three-argument memset_explicit API

memset_explicit takes a destination, fill byte and byte count, unlike
memset_s which also takes the destination size. Newer glibc releases
provide memset_explicit, exposing the invalid call in rep_memset_s when
building the Samba host tools. Keep the existing bounds checks and the
fallback for systems without memset_explicit.

--- a/lib/replace/replace.c
+++ b/lib/replace/replace.c
@@ -972,3 +972,3 @@ int rep_memset_s(void *dest, size_t destsz,
 #if defined(HAVE_MEMSET_EXPLICIT)
-	memset_explicit(dest, destsz, ch, count);
+	memset_explicit(dest, ch, count);
 #else /* HAVE_MEMSET_EXPLICIT */
